{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/402696-recs-for-orpheus","id":402696,"title":"Recs for Orpheus?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-11T18:21:42-08:00","id":402696,"title":"Recs for Orpheus?","content":"How was <b>Orpheus</b>? It came out right after my local source for White Wolf closed, so I never had a chance to see any of the books, or get a feel for the campaign (although the trailer looks cool). Did it turn out well? Any particular strengths, weaknesses, or clever ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T21:26:09-08:00","id":402967,"title":"","content":"I think all around Orpheus is a pretty strong game. It was very different for a cWOD game because it did a very decent job of balancing having what a metaplot really should be if you're going to do one (there is a planned out set of events that unfolds over the course of the books with focus and purposeful introduction of mechanical issues as well as setting ones) with a game that still works if you want to toss the metaplot out. You don't get stuck with playing the core Orpheus arc out once and then have nothing left to do with it.<br /> <br /> It's a cWOD game, so it has some of the standard caveat mechanical features/bugs that come with that. But as a late Revised book that base line mechanics are generally solid.<br /> <br /> There's some clever stuff in the creation mechanics as Nature if very important in Orpheus to work as an additional &quot;splat&quot; on top of your Shade (what kind of ghostly &quot;spirit&quot; you have) and Lament (how your character interacts with the world of ghosts). Your primary traits are Vitality, Spite, and Willpower, and the combination of splats you take dictate their starting values.<br /> <br /> However character creation with Orpheus can be disappointing (though easily fixed) as Orpheus PCs have the worst starting spreads. They get mortal Attributes and Abilities, less base Backgrounds than anyone else, and supernatural (15) freebies. I'd advise either upping their freebies to 21 (makes up for the low starting Backgrounds more easily that giving them supernatural creation stat Attributes/Abilities). It feels really easy to run out of dots compared to the other games. If you're used to the other cWOD games, and want to run Orpheus without house rules first, just be ready to tone concepts back from what you'd assume is a decent starting level character.<br /> <br /> The overall mechanics of Orpheus are decent. Like any first edition of a game, there's some bugs in it. Orpheus is more like Hunter where the PCs aren't going to amass many individual powers, but unlike Hunter a lot of their powers are very versatile depending on how much juice you want to put into them.<br /> <br /> Also like Hunter, Orpheus really stands apart from the rest of the cWOD. It's not really set up for crossovers with the larger setting, but again unlike Hunter it at least meshes much more easily with the other game lines setting-wise. Though the implications of Orpheus would have pretty drastic implications for many of the other supernaturals (since Orpheus operates openly as a company that employs astral projecting and dead agents).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T07:42:50-08:00","id":403312,"title":"","content":"The adventure sourcebooks offer a lot of suggestions on different ways the plot can go depending on the players' interests and decisions, so you could use a lot of the adventures even if (for example) the big twist in <b>Crusade Of Ashes</b> doesn't happen. You'll still need to do some work if the group veers wildly away from the basic plot, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T08:23:21-08:00","id":404485,"title":"","content":"I would wholeheartedly recommend Orpheus. They are very well written, and I enjoy reading the books even if I'm not going to be using much out of them at the moment. The metaplot is fun to use, but it is also very easy to ignore in favor of your own stories if you wish to do something else with a game. It has a very interesting style of play that lends itself well to a group, though you'll want some NPCs around if you are running it for just a single player. The powers of the different characters can actually be combined together for greater effects, so you'd need the extra characters around to get the most mileage out of that. Each book in the series brought out new potential allies and antagonists along with mechanical details to support them. While the core book gave five Shades (the Nature-based 'types' of ghosts), the supplements provided two new 'natural Shades' and one 'unnatural Shade' (in the form of the Orphan-Grinders - ghosts who clawed their way back from Spectre-hood). My one problem with that system was that it seemed to leave out an 8th 'natural Shade' to go with the more negative Natures, but it did leave it open for people to either assume that those Natures corresponded more to Spectres, or to create one of their own (as I did here: <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Orpheus/PF/Wraith_Shade_and_Horrors.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...nd_Horrors.pdf</a> ).<br /> <br /> To put it into your original framework:<br /> \u200b<br /> Yes, it turned out well.<br /> <br /> Strengths: Flavorful and potent powers that encourage teamwork with mechanical bonuses. The antagonists are well thought out and sufficiently frightening for a good horror game. Each supplement expands the scope of the game with new settings, characters, and mechanics. Ghosts are legitimate threats to the living and dead alike, as all but the weakest can make their presence felt to the living.<br /> <br /> Weaknesses: Not very crossover friendly with any other World of Darkness games. To get all the juicy mechanics available for the game, you need all the supplements (though if someone is like me, the first one will give more than enough to make that seem like a worthwhile investment).<br /> <br /> Clever ideas: Large corporations that openly deal with ghostly phenomena. A soul-damaging illegal drug that allows its users to see ghosts. A ghostly world that ghosts can no longer safely enter, leaving them trapped closer to mankind than they've ever been before.<br /> <br /> I hope this has been helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}